#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:1
msgid "Abundance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:3
msgid ""
"The abundance contains information about the overall metallicity of the "
"star as well as the individual abundances of each element. SME can "
"simulate and fit the first 99 elements of the periodic table (from "
"Hydrogen H to Einsteinium Es)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:9
msgid "Abundance formats"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:11
msgid ""
"PySME supports a variety of formats to input the abundance. However they "
"are all internally converted to the 'H=12' type before use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:15
msgid "H=12"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:17
msgid ""
"Abundance values are log10 of the fraction of nuclei of each element in "
"any form relative to the number of hydrogen in any form plus an offset of"
" 12. For the Sun, the nuclei abundance values of H, He, and Li are "
"approximately 12, 10.9, and 1.05."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:23
msgid "n/nTot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:24
msgid ""
"Abundance values are the fraction of nuclei of each element in any form "
"relative to the total for all elements in any form. For the Sun, the "
"abundance values of H, He, and Li are approximately 0.92, 0.078, and "
"1.03e-11."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:29
msgid "n/nH"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:30
msgid ""
"Abundance values are the fraction of nuclei of each element in any form "
"relative to the number of hydrogen nuclei in any form. For the Sun, the "
"abundance values of H, He, and Li are approximately 1, 0.085, and "
"1.12e-11."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:36
msgid "sme"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:37
msgid ""
"For hydrogen, the abundance value is the fraction of all nuclei that are "
"hydrogen, including all ionization states and treating molecules as "
"constituent atoms. For the other elements, the abundance values are log10"
" of the fraction of nuclei of each element in any form relative to the "
"total for all elements in any form. For the Sun, the abundance values of "
"H, He, and Li are approximately 0.92, -1.11, and -11.0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:45
msgid "Fe=12"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:46
msgid ""
"Abundance values are log10 of the fraction of nuclei of each element in "
"any form relative to the number of iron in any form plus an offset of 12."
" For the Sun, the nuclei abundance values of H, He, and Li are "
"approximately 16.5, 15.43, and 5.55."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:52
msgid "n/nFe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:53
msgid ""
"Abundance values are the fraction of nuclei of each element in any form "
"relative to the number of iron nuclei in any form. For the Sun, the "
"abundance values of H, He, and Li are approximately 3.16e4, 2.69e3, and "
"3.55e-7."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:59
msgid "Solar metallicity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:61
msgid ""
"PySME contains multiple pre defined sets of solar abundances for you to "
"choose from. They are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:64
msgid "From solar photosphere:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:65
msgid ""
"`anders1989`: [Anders & Grevesse (1989, "
"GeCoA)](https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/1989GeCoA..53..197A)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:66
msgid ""
"`grevesse1996`: [Grevesse, Noels & Sauval (1996, "
"ASPC)](https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/1996ASPC...99..117G)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:67
msgid ""
"`grevesse1998`: [Grevesse, & Sauval (1998, "
"SSRv)](https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/1998SSRv...85..161G)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:68
msgid ""
"`asplund2005`: [Asplund, Grevesse & Sauval (2005, "
"ASPC)](https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2005ASPC..336...25A)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:69
msgid ""
"`grevesse2007` (alias: `solar`): [Grevesse, Asplund & Sauval (2007, "
"SSRv)](https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2007SSRv..130..105G)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:70
msgid ""
"`asplund2009`: [Asplund, Grevesse & Sauval (2009, "
"ARA&A)](https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2009ARA&A..47..481A)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:71
msgid ""
"`asplund2021`: [Asplund, Amarsi & Grevesse (2021, "
"A&A)](https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2021A&A...653A.141A)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:73
msgid "From CI chondrites:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:74
msgid ""
"`lodders2003`: [Lodders(2003 "
"ApJ)](https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2003ApJ...591.1220L)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:75
msgid ""
"`lodders2010`: [Lodders(2010 "
"ASSP)](https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2010ASSP...16..379L)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:77
msgid ""
"They can be initialized by passing their name during the creation of the "
"abundance. E.g. Abund(\"grevesse2007\"). The default solar abundance is "
"'grevesse2007' and is also available using Abund.solar()."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:82
msgid "Conversions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:84
msgid "sme -> H=12"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:86 ../../concepts/abundance.md:103
msgid "We have:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:87
msgid ""
"$S_\\mathrm{H} = \\frac{N_\\mathrm{H}}{N_\\mathrm{all}}$ for Hydrogen in "
"`sme` scale;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:88
msgid ""
"$S_\\mathrm{X} = \\log{\\frac{N_\\mathrm{X}}{N_\\mathrm{all}}}$ for "
"element $\\mathrm{X}$ other than Hydrogen in `sme` scale;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:89 ../../concepts/abundance.md:107
#, python-brace-format
msgid "$H_\\mathrm{H} = 12$ for Hydrogen in `H=12` scale;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:90 ../../concepts/abundance.md:108
msgid ""
"$H_\\mathrm{X} = \\log{\\frac{N_\\mathrm{X}}{N_\\mathrm{H}}} + 12$ for "
"element $\\mathrm{X}$ other than Hydrogen in `H=12` scale."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:92 ../../concepts/abundance.md:110
msgid "thus"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:94
msgid "$H_\\mathrm{X} = S_\\mathrm{X} - \\log{S_\\mathrm{H}}$"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:96
msgid "H=12 -> sme"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:98
msgid ""
"$S_\\mathrm{H} = \\left[1 + \\sum_\\mathrm{X}{10^{H_\\mathrm{X}-12}} "
"\\right]^{-1}$"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:99
msgid "$S_\\mathrm{X} = \\log{(S_\\mathrm{H} \\times 10^{H_\\mathrm{X}-12})}$"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:101
msgid "kurucz -> H=12"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:104
msgid ""
"$K_\\mathrm{H} = \\frac{N_\\mathrm{H}}{N_\\mathrm{all}}$ for Hydrogen in "
"`kurucz` scale;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:105
msgid ""
"$K_\\mathrm{He} = \\frac{N_\\mathrm{He}}{N_\\mathrm{all}}$ for Helium in "
"`kurucz` scale;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:106
msgid ""
"$K_\\mathrm{X} = "
"\\log{\\frac{N_\\mathrm{X}}{N_\\mathrm{H}+N_\\mathrm{He}}}$ for element "
"$\\mathrm{X}$ other than H and He in `kurucz` scale;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:112
msgid "$H_\\mathrm{He} = \\log{\\frac{K_\\mathrm{He}}{K_\\mathrm{H}}} + 12$"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:113
msgid ""
"$H_\\mathrm{X} = K_\\mathrm{X} + "
"\\log{\\left(\\frac{K_\\mathrm{He}}{K_\\mathrm{H}} + 1\\right)} + 12$"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:115
msgid "H=12 -> kurucz"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:117
msgid ""
"$K_\\mathrm{H} = \\left(1 + \\sum_\\mathrm{X}10^{H_\\mathrm{X}-12} "
"\\right)^{-1}$"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:118
msgid ""
"$K_\\mathrm{He} = \\left(10^{12-H_\\mathrm{He}} + 1 + "
"10^{12-H_\\mathrm{He}}\\times\\sum_\\mathrm{X}10^{H_\\mathrm{X}-12} "
"\\right)^{-1}$"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/abundance.md:119
msgid "$K_\\mathrm{X} = H_\\mathrm{X}-12-\\log{(1+10^{H_\\mathrm{He}-12})}$"
msgstr ""

